From 2e70d5cef7668b98bfe12fdf699a994dceb626a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:41:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MUMPSSolver: fixes of an independent review of ReuseAnalysis

- the solver is moved to an internal header (src/MUMPSSolvers.hxx) and
  renamed MUMPSSolverReusingAnalysis; it keeps its communicator for the
  reduction and only has the constructor taking a communicator;
- the pattern of the new matrix is compared in place, without any
  allocation before the collective reduction, and only copied after a
  new analysis;
- the stored pattern is forgotten while MUMPS analyses and factorizes the
  new matrix: if this fails by an exception (MFEM built with exceptions),
  the next matrix is analysed again instead of being factorized with an
  analysis of another pattern;
- the number of analyses made is counted and given by the new function
  getNumberOfMUMPSAnalyses;
- MUMPSReuseAnalysisTest checks the number of analyses after each
  operator (an analysis made if and only if the pattern changed), with a
  case where only the global indices of the off-diagonal columns change
  on all processes (MUMPS crashed or blocked when this comparison was
  removed, without failure of the previous test), two successive reuses,
  a right-hand side which is not uniform, operators destroyed after their
  local blocks are no longer used, and a time limit; the test, which uses
  no behaviour, is declared with the tests of the linear solvers;
- documentation: the analysis of MUMPS only depends on the pattern of the
  matrix, which MFEM gives distributed (no maximum transversal
  permutation, scaling computed at each factorization).

Seven mutations of the solver are detected by the test (no comparison,
no reduction, global indices or column indices of the off-diagonal block
not compared, never reused, pattern forgotten after a reuse, analyses not
counted).
